    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="ve_d24">

                <pb facs="ve_d24-1" n="1" xml:id="ve_d24-1"/>

                <head>VE–24. Telegram from the Ambassador in Venezuela (Sparks) to the Department of
                        State<anchor n="1" xml:id="ve_d24-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1959-03-30T19:00:00-05:00">March 30, 1959, 7
                            p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>566. Saturday papers front paged INS stories
                    order that Perez Jimenez and family leave U.S. by April 15, possibility appeal
                    noted but general impression is Perez Jimenez will depart. UP and AP reported
                    State Department supports INS order and that
                    his expulsion is in U.S. interests.</p>
                <pb facs="1346" n="1258" type="typeset" xml:id="pg1258"/>
                <p>Editorial and cartoon comment hall move EL NACIONAL comments “if they really
                    expel Perez Jimenez, welcome Mr. Nixon” EL INDEPENDIENTE editorial welcomes
                    change of policy of support toward Perez Jimenez and other dictators although
                    considering it overdue follow up stories report Perez Jimenez planning go Spain
                    or Dominican Republic.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Sparks</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
